  "contentYjsBase64": "",
  "contentPlaintext": "<bold>👋 Getting Started</bold>\nWelcome to the development team. This central guide serves as the single source of truth for our product workflows, delivery processes, and codebase standards.\n<bold>1. Table of Contents</bold>\n1. Table of Contents\n2. Workspace Ecosystem & Team Roles\n3. Workspace Directory Structure\n4. Agile Delivery Process & Sprints\n5. Task Label Taxonomy & Priority Matrix\n6. Engineering & Operational Baseline Rules\n<bold>2. Workspace Ecosystem & Team Roles</bold>\nThis workspace uses functional role levels to protect configuration settings, streamline delivery, and keep external partners informed without cluttering operational boards.\nRole\nWorkspace Label\nOperational Scope & Accountabilities\nPermission Layer\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">OWNER</textStyle></bold>\nOwner\nProduct strategy, commercial goals, system configurations.\nFull Access / Admin Control\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">ADMIN</textStyle></bold>\nEngineering Manager\nEngineering health, resource allocation, workflow grooming.\nFull Access / Configuration\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">MANAGER</textStyle></bold>\nTech Lead\nArchitecture design, PR validations, technical roadmaps.\nWrite + Moderate Boards\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">MEMBER</textStyle></bold>\nDeveloper\nCode delivery, test automation, asset documentation.\nWrite + Edit Task Assets\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">VIEWER</textStyle></bold>\nStakeholder\nRoadmap progress reviews, feedback input, spec evaluation.\nRead-Only + Comments\n<bold>3. Workspace Directory Structure</bold>\nThe repository workspace uses a standardized layout. Do not create unapproved root folders:\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">🎯 Product</textStyle></bold>: Contains product strategy, market metrics, PRDs, and active milestone timelines.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">⚙️ Engineering</textStyle></bold>: Technical documentation, system architecture patterns, and setups.\n<italic>🏗️ Architecture</italic>: High-level component patterns and interface maps.\n<italic>📋 Architecture Decisions</italic>: Historical collection of Architectural Decision Records (ADRs).\n<italic>📖 Runbooks</italic>: On-call steps, deployment paths, and recovery steps.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">🔄 Processes</textStyle></bold>: Team operating rules, development standards, and recurring meeting logs.\n<italic>🔁 Retrospectives</italic>: Retrospective logs from our 2-week agile delivery cycles.\n<italic>🗓️ Meeting Notes</italic>: Standup updates, design reviews, and cross-team meetings.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">🎨 Design</textStyle></bold>: UI assets, visual component frameworks, design specs, and user journeys.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">👋 Onboarding</textStyle></bold>: Setup guides, environment variables, and introductory material for new team members.\n<bold>4. Agile Delivery Process & Sprints</bold>\nOur product development runs on fixed <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">2-week sprint cycles</textStyle></bold>. Tasks move through our kanban pipeline columns using strict workflow rules:\n[ Backlog ] ➔ [ Sprint Todo ] ➔ [ In Progress ] ➔ [ PR / Review ] ➔ [ Done ]\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Backlog</textStyle></bold>: Prioritized product ideas and engineering tasks. These are groomed but not yet scheduled.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Sprint</textStyle></bold>: The committed task bundle for the active 2-week cycle. No new tasks are added mid-sprint without explicit manager approval.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">In Progress</textStyle></bold>: Active execution tasks. Engineers should focus on exactly one ticket at a time to optimize delivery speeds.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">PR / Review</textStyle></bold>: Code completed and awaiting peer review, or design specs awaiting validation. All items require two developer approvals.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Done</textStyle></bold>: Code merged, passing automated tests, and deployed to production.\n<bold>5. Task Label Taxonomy & Priority Matrix</bold>\nEvery ticket added to the tracking boards must use a standard taxonomy tag to keep development boards highly scannable:\n🟢 <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">feature</textStyle></bold>: New business logic, user stories, interface updates, or public API endpoints.\n🔴 <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">bug</textStyle></bold>: System errors, broken logic, regression anomalies, or platform edge-case failures.\n⚫ <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">chore</textStyle></bold>: Technical debt remediation, dependency updates, or pipeline configuration updates.\n🔵 <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">spike</textStyle></bold>: Timed exploration blocks, performance benchmarking, or architectural research.\n⚪ <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">blocked</textStyle></bold>: Progress stopped by an external dependency, third-party api access, or open product decisions.\n🚨 <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">p0</textStyle></bold>: Critical system crash. Drops everything else to resolve immediately.\n🔶 <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">p1</textStyle></bold>: High business value task or severe functional bottleneck. Schedule for the active sprint.\n🍇 <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">good-first-issue</textStyle></bold>: Low-complexity starter tasks optimized for new developers joining the team.\n<bold>6. Engineering & Operational Baseline Rules</bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Groom Weekly</textStyle></bold>: Ensure the Backlog folder contains detailed context, mock data references, and explicit acceptance parameters before moving items to the Sprint board.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">No Ghost Decisions</textStyle></bold>: Major technical changes require a written Architecture Decision Record (ADR) file added to the matching system directory within 24 hours of agreement.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Document Incidents</textStyle></bold>: Any production stability breakdown must be logged with an Incident Postmortem report to help prevent future stability bugs.",
